    "result_text": "The build is green and all references are cleaned up. The task is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Format** (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`):\n- **REGION** \u2014 region code from postcode/city (`NSW`)\n- **FY** \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date (`27`)\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (`16E6609E`), the same hash used by the region-and-hash identity\n- **CHK** \u2014 single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` (`1`)\n\n**Changes made:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode` + `checkDigit` with a `memberId` schema property; removed `membershipNumber` (DTOs are generated from this spec).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields + accessors and the `getCheckDigit()` method; added the persisted `memberId` field + accessors.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `generateCustomerCode`/`generateMembershipNumber` with `generateMemberId` (plus a `luhnCheckDigit` helper); collision de-duplication now runs against `memberId` (appending `-<n>`); the human-readable audit line and the structured event now carry `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 renamed the primary-identifier field from `customerCode` to `memberId`.\n- **`LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 `forCustomerCode`/`timezoneForCustomerCode` renamed to `forMemberId`/`timezoneForMemberId`; region is now parsed as the leading alphabetic prefix of the concatenated `memberId` (no `-` separator); `ownerSegment` references the memberId.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the locality/timezone/ownerSegment expressions to pass `getMemberId()`.\n- **DB schemas** (all 4 dialects) \u2014 replaced `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns with a single `member_id`; fixed the positional hsqldb seed inserts to match the new column count.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The `AcceptanceTest` confirms the returned `memberId` starts with `NSW`, contains the computed HASH8, and that the old `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields are gone.",
